# The root R0 without an entry. The ambiguity is that of the path alone (the coordinates of Sol and Astra for the row
# construction_path_ambiguous), on ordinary Structures: C is written directly in D and declares the reference `p` by
# the path `S\f`, where S holds two Structures named f. `call(code := D\C)` selects the code by naming its formal --
# nothing is opened --; the path `S\f` is reached when the record runs and is ambiguous: 3. The label is written
# immediately before it: `Log\before` 1, `Log\after` 0.
@: Log (int: before 0; int: after 0)
@: D (S(f(int: v 11); f(int: v 12)); C(@: p S\f))
Log\before := 1
call(code := D\C)
Log\after := 1
